  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q8",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "$a$ is inversely proportional to $b^2$. If $a=8$ when $b=2$, find:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$a$ when $b=4$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=2$.",
          "worked": "Since $a\\propto \\frac{1}{b^2}$, write $a=\\frac{k}{b^2}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}k&=ab^2\\\\k&=8\\times2^2\\\\k&=32\\end{align*}$$\nHence $a=\\frac{32}{b^2}$. When $b=4$,\n$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{32}{4^2}\\\\a&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$b$ when $a=9$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$b=\\pm\\dfrac{4\\sqrt2}{3}$.\n\nUse $ab^2=32$ and take both square roots.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}k&=8\\times2^2\\\\k&=32\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $a=\\frac{32}{b^2}$ when $a=9$,\n$$\\begin{align*}9&=\\frac{32}{b^2}\\\\b^2&=\\frac{32}{9}\\\\b&=\\pm\\sqrt{\\frac{32}{9}}\\\\b&=\\pm\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{3}.\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs satisfy $a=\\frac{32}{b^2}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 58
      }
    ]
  },
